Certainly! Here's a simple JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  const adjectives = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
    if (words[i].match(/^(beautiful|green)$/)) {
      adjectives.push(words[i]);
    }
  }

  if (adjectives.length > 1) {
    const firstAdjective = adjectives.shift();
    adjectives.push(firstAdjective);
    const newSentence = adjectives.join(" ") + " " + words.filter(word => !word.match(/^(beautiful|green)$/)).join(" ");
    return newSentence;
  } else {
    return sentence;
  }
}

const inputSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const outputSentence = switchAdjectives(inputSentence);
console.log(outputSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function splits the input sentence into individual words, filters out the adjectives ("beautiful" and "green"), and then rearranges them in the desired order. If there are no adjectives in the sentence, it simply returns the original sentence unchanged.

